hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16725","Abu Asim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi, he said: a freedman of Yazid ibn Nimran narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Nimran narrated to me, he said: I met a paralyzed, long-haired man and asked him; he said: I passed in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a she-ass or a donkey, and he said: He cut off our prayer, may Allah cut off his trace; so I was made paralyzed."
